:\"The command trace shows a normal discovery-then-iterate pattern with no unnecessary or unreverted mutations. cmd-fc1fed943da7463a partially failed only because openssl 1.0.2 lacks -addext; the CA working directory and private key it created were retained and successfully reused by the next command (cmd-ab1ea986fbf04e6d) rather than being abandoned, so this is a corrective retry, not wasted state. Several subsequent commands (cmd-b0efb07b28f34675, cmd-8d11bfa1a7ef45b5, cmd-7950c17dd8574406) returned nonzero exit codes, but these were read-only verification/diagnostic steps failing due to permission or subshell quirks under sudo -n, not state-changing actions, and they were promptly corrected (e.g., cmd-3121c441fdf14608 re-runs the failed health check with proper sudo prefixing and succeeds). The single genuinely state-changing sequence (key/cert generation, install, update-ca-certificates, reboot) is fully tied to the task outcome or the mandated restart protocol, and the lifecycle diff shows only the expected boot-identity and systemd-private tmp-dir churn from the reboot, with no residue, failed services, new listening sockets, or package-health issues introduced.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-fc1fed943da7463a\",\"cmd-ab1ea986fbf04e6d\",\"cmd-b0efb07b28f34675\",\"cmd-8d11bfa1a7ef45b5\",\"cmd-7950c17dd8574406\",\"cmd-3121c441fdf14608\",\"global:after_executor:node1:failed-services\",\"global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets\",\"global:after_executor:node1:package-health\"]},\"overall_summary\":\"Both material outcomes of the task — creating a CA named 'OS Comparison Root CA' and installing it as a trusted system CA on node1 — are directly and coherently supported by evidence: certificate generation with the correct subject/CA extensions, successful update-ca-certificates run, presence of the PEM and hash symlinks in the system trust store, and openssl verify succeeding via the default trust store. The independently-required node-restart evidence protocol is als